# proto-file: googlesql/compliance/known_error.proto
# proto-message: KnownErrorFile
#
# Compliance tests the emulator is known to fail. Remove an entry once its tests pass.

# The emulator rejects what it does not support as unsupported, which clients can tell apart from
# BigQuery's behavior: any statement may fail as UNIMPLEMENTED. A wrong result, or an error where
# BigQuery succeeds, still fails the test.
known_errors {
  mode: ALLOW_UNIMPLEMENTED
  reason: "The emulator rejects what it does not support"
  label: ".*"
}

# BigQuery generates arrays far longer than GoogleSQL's 16000 elements, so the emulator lifts the
# limit, and these ranges of about 1e38 BIGNUMERIC elements run for most of an hour each before
# they fail, as the tests expect, with or without SAFE. They are not run.
known_errors {
  mode: CRASHES_DO_NOT_RUN
  reason: "GENERATE_ARRAY over a BIGNUMERIC range too long to generate"
  label: "code:(safe_error_mode__safe_)?generate_array_BIGNUMERIC_0_BIGNUMERIC_1_BIGNUMERIC_0.00000000000000000000000000000000000001"
  label: "code:(safe_error_mode__safe_)?generate_array_BIGNUMERIC_-578960446186580977117854925043439539266.34992332820282019728792003956564819968_BIGNUMERIC_578960446186580977117854925043439539266.34992332820282019728792003956564819967_BIGNUMERIC_1"
}
